From 9b4299917976b0184d097bfae8b65f7600c5d4b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Red Daka <emmanuel.rayan.daka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:46:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove unrelated files accidentally committed in a prior
 merge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PR #2 (merged as 68f0b3e) swept in ~2MB / 207 files that have nothing to
do with this project, alongside its intended changes:

- british_english_3_3_17/ and japanese_3_3_17/ — a full phpBB 3.3.17
  forum-software translation pack (PHP language files, icons,
  stylesheets). A leftover `note` file in the same commit shows this was
  the residue of an unrelated conversation about sourcing i18n strings
  from a phpBB ZIP — the extracted archive got committed instead of
  just the strings.
- i18next and react-i18next in package.json — added as part of that
  same exploration, confirmed unused anywhere in src/. Removed and
  package-lock.json regenerated accordingly.
- Three stray *.patch files that were left in the repo root after being
  applied with `git am` in earlier sessions and then accidentally
  tracked by a blanket `git add`/commit.
- The `note` file itself.

None of this was harmful at runtime (phpBB's PHP files aren't executed
by this app, nothing imports the i18n packages), but it doesn't belong
in the repository or its history going forward.

Verified: `tsc --noEmit`, `eslint`, and `vite build` all pass clean
after removal, with the same pre-existing Prettier-only lint count as
before (1290) — confirming nothing load-bearing was accidentally
removed alongside the unrelated files.
